# fraim system jobs. Baked into the image and updated with every release.
# Owners and their Claude make automations in ~/fraim/automations instead; this file is read-only.

# Pick up new or changed automations in ~/fraim/automations within a minute.
* * * * * fraim-auto sync --quiet

# Health check every hour; WhatsApp only when something breaks or recovers.
0 * * * * fraim-doctor --notify

# Every hour: a question nobody answered in time (expire_hours, default 72) counts as no.
30 * * * * fraim-queue expire

# Every 10 minutes: learn from the owner's chats once they pause (stated preferences become
# rules at once, corrections wait in the queue). Does nothing, and costs nothing, without new messages.
*/10 * * * * fraim-brain review --quiet

# Every Sunday evening: propose rule changes from new review feedback; the owner approves them in the queue.
0 20 * * 0 fraim-brain distill --if-new

# Every morning: one queue card when a default the owner has their own copy of changed.
0 9 * * * fraim-prompt stale --notify

# Every Monday: tell the owner once when a new fraimwork release is available.
0 10 * * 1 fraim-version-check --notify

# Every night: clean up after ended goals. After a day their checkouts lose installed packages
# and their terminals close; after a week checkouts whose work is on GitHub go, and so do the
# goals' work folders (the report stays).
15 4 * * * fraim-goal prune

# Every Sunday night: empty the npm download cache (goals refill it; it grows by gigabytes).
45 4 * * 0 npm cache clean --force >/dev/null 2>&1
